---
const views = [
  { name: "The map", body: "The component graph, then every component, symbol and file: what depends on it, its tests, and what a change would break." },
  { name: "Changes", body: "What your uncommitted work means, or any two refs, with the lane it takes and why." },
  { name: "Decisions", body: "Submit to the judge, run tests in environments, answer escalations, read the audit log, and follow each agent's track record week by week." },
];
---

<section class="chapter dashboard" id="dashboard" data-phase="6" aria-labelledby="dashboard-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chapter-copy wide">
      <h2 class="display-l" id="dashboard-title">All of it, in your browser.</h2>
      <p class="body-l">
        <code class="code">onus ui</code> opens the whole of Onus for the repository you are in. It ships inside the binary
        and serves on 127.0.0.1 behind a per-session token, so nothing is installed and nothing leaves your machine.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="shot">
      <div class="frame">
        <div class="bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><code>127.0.0.1:4387/changes</code></div>
        <img
          src="/screens/changes-dark.webp"
          width="1920"
          height="1200"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          alt="The Onus web interface reporting a change: four changes in meaning, one needing a person because customer phone numbers now leave the system through a new SMS vendor, and the lane it takes."
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="caption muted">
        A 1,408-line pull request, read as four changes in meaning. The one that sends phone numbers to a new vendor comes first, and the change goes to a person.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul class="views">
      {
        views.map((v) => (
          <li>
            <h3 class="title">{v.name}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{v.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .dashboard > .wrap {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(var(--space-6), 1.5rem + 2vw, var(--space-8));
  }

  .wide {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .shot {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .frame {
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 12%, transparent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-window);
    background: #0e1a24;
  }

  .bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 10%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 80%, transparent);
  }

  .bar span {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 22%, transparent);
  }

  .bar code {
    margin-left: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .frame img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .views {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .views li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .views .title {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
  }
</style>
